# Environment names as tagteam classifies them (spec 15.4): every CLAUDE_CODE_* and
# ANTHROPIC_* name tagteam knows, and every name `run` scrubs (spec 12.5).
#
# Format: one entry per line, "<class> <NAME>"; blank lines and lines starting with '#' are
# ignored, as in known-shared. A NAME is upper-case letters, digits and '_'; each '*' in it
# matches any run of characters, possibly empty, against the whole name. Classes:
#   scrub  `run` removes it from a session's environment (CC_SCRUB, spec 12.5), and doctor
#          warns when one is set (spec 13.6)
#   known  classified as harmless to a session: `run` passes it through
# The weekly drift job (scripts/cc-drift.sh) reports each CLAUDE_CODE_* and ANTHROPIC_* name
# in the latest claude that no entry matches. Classify each one here.

